    "title": "How We Verify Every Tradesperson on Our Platform",
    "content": "**Trust is everything in an emergency. Inviting a stranger into your home when you are vulnerable requires confidence that they are who they say they are.**\r\n\r\nAt **Emergency Tradesmen**, we don't just list anyone with a van. We employ a rigorous 6-step verification process to ensure every tradesperson on our platform is qualified, insured, and legitimate. Here is exactly how we vet our network.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 1. Identity & Company Checks (Level 1)\r\nBefore a tradesperson can join, we verify their legal identity.\r\n*   **Photo ID:** Passport or Driving Licence upload.\r\n*   **Company Registration:** We check Companies House (UK) or State Business Registries (US) to ensure the LTD/LLC is active and solvent.\r\n*   **Address Verification:** Utility bill proof of trading address. We do not accept PO Boxes.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 2. Qualification Verification (Level 2)\r\nSkills matter. A handyman cannot fix a boiler.\r\n*   **Gas Safe Register (UK):** We check their licence number against the Gas Safe database in real-time. If it's expired, they are suspended immediately.\r\n*   **NICEIC / NAPIT (Electrical):** We verify their \"Competent Person Scheme\" membership for Part P compliance.\r\n*   **City & Guilds / NVQ:** We request certificates for standard plumbing and carpentry trades.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 3. Public Liability Insurance (Level 3)\r\nAccidents happen. If a plumber floods your home, who pays?\r\n*   **The Check:** We require proof of valid Public Liability Insurance (Minimum ┬ú2 Million cover).\r\n*   **The Purpose:** This protects you, the homeowner, from bearing the cost of accidental damage caused during the repair.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 4. Criminal Record Checks (Level 4)\r\nSafety is paramount.\r\n*   **DBS Check (UK):** We encourage Enhanced DBS checks for locksmiths and trades entering homes with vulnerable people.\r\n*   **Background Screen:** We screen for major red flags.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 5. The \"Real Work\" Audit (Level 5)\r\nPaperwork is one thing; quality is another.\r\n*   **Portfolio Review:** We review photos of past work.\r\n*   **Customer Feedback:** We monitor reviews on Trustpilot, Google, and our internal system.\r\n*   **Three Strikes Rule:** If a tradesperson receives 3 substantiated complaints about quality or conduct (e.g., ghosting, rudeness, overcharging), they are permanently removed from the platform.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## 6. Price Transparency Promise\r\nWe fight against \"Cowboy Pricing.\" \r\n*   **No Hidden Fees:** Our partners agree to a transparent pricing structure.\r\n*   **Quote Before Work:** You must agree to the price *before* tools are picked up.\r\n*   **VAT Invoices:** All trades must provide a proper tax invoice.\r\n\r\n---\r\n\r\n## Summary\r\nOur badge isn't just a logo; it's a shield. When you use **Emergency Tradesmen**, you are hiring a professional who has passed strict vetting to earn their place. **Safety. Quality. Accountability.** That is our promise.\r\n"
